		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Re: Modification of the Radioditty charger with &quot;TP5100&quot; card at $ 2.]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=564&amp;p=36484#p36484"><![CDATA[
I have mod my RD-5R charger and set the charging current to 1 A (RTS = 0.1 Ohm). Trying with the original power supply (10V 0.5A) the battery was being charged at 0.6A. When switched to a 12V 3A power supply, the battery was being charged at 1 A. I then switched back to original power supply and completed the charge on the test battery. Everything was well, the power supply is in the normal temp.<br><br>In conclusion, If the selected charging current is more than the power supply can provide, the module will charge at maximum current it can, nothing damage.<br><br>With 12V 3A power supply<div class="inline-attachment"><dl class="file"><dt class="attach-image"><img src="http://localhost/opengd77/download/file.php?id=2891&amp;sid=2de05a30036f75ec9e9eb1c1c27ca24d" class="postimage" alt="IMG_2029.jpeg" onclick="viewableArea(this);" /></dt></dl></div>With original power supply (10V 0.5A)<div class="inline-attachment"><dl class="file"><dt class="attach-image"><img src="http://localhost/opengd77/download/file.php?id=2892&amp;sid=2de05a30036f75ec9e9eb1c1c27ca24d" class="postimage" alt="IMG_2028.jpeg" onclick="viewableArea(this);" /></dt></dl></div>I have also brought RED/BLUE common Anode LED for this project from Amazon. It's come in a pack of 200 LEDs, so If anyone in the US would like to have some, I will mail 10 of them to you for $1.<div class="inline-attachment"><dl class="file"><dt class="attach-image"><img src="http://localhost/opengd77/download/file.php?id=2893&amp;sid=2de05a30036f75ec9e9eb1c1c27ca24d" class="postimage" alt="IMG_2037-EDIT.jpg" onclick="viewableArea(this);" /></dt></dl></div>Thank you everyone in this thread. Great information, fun project.<br>Charlie,<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=5068">KA1CM</a> — Wed Mar 26, 2025 9:56 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
